Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:33:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 317/407] Unified: a hole on a round end goes to its centre; a
 hole across a round face

- Hole on a flat face clicked near the middle of a round end or eye (half
  its radius): at the circle's centre. A connecting rod's eye could not
  be given a centred hole; a sketch and a pocket were made instead.
- Hole on a cylindrical outside face (a piston's pin hole): the bar offers
  it, and it goes in along the face's normal at the click. Before, it was
  not offered (0.7.3) or went the wrong way (0.6.9).
(engine field test 0.7.3)

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestSnapMath, -t TestContextRules

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
